 "text": "Reference\nAudit Observations\nAudit Recommendations\n2.9.1, 2. Coordinate with the City General\nServices Office as to status of deliveries of\ngoods and services and recognize the\ncorresponding liability If no payment had\nbeen made; and\n2.9.1.3. Maintain a separate SL for each\ncontractor/suppller for proper monitoring of\neach outstanding payable and status of\naccounts.\n2.9.2. The City General Service Office to\npromptly Inform the OCAT of deliveries of\nprocured goods and services and furnish the\nlatter with required documents to support\nthe timely recording of transactions.\nAAR 2023\n3. Insufficient Imposition of RPT and SET by the The Office of the City Assessor -\nObservation No. 3 City due to: 1) misplaced application of the\nPage 85\nAssessment Levels (ALs) prescribed under\nSection 12 of Ordinance No. 8331, s.Serles of\n2013;; and 2) omission of 1,130 RPUs In the\nAssessment Rolls (AR) contrary to Section 2,\nChapter II, Manual on Real Property Appraisal\nand Assessment Operations (MRPAAO),, thereby\ndiminishing the City's earnings to be utilized to\nfinance Its programs/projects/activities (PPAs).\n3.16.1.1. Ensure that Assessment Levels and\nAssessed Values are accurately computed\nand provided;\nAGENCY ACTION PLAN\nStatus of\nPerson/Dept\nAction Plan\nResponsible\nTarget Implementation Date\nFrom\nImplementation\nTo\nReason for Partial/Delay/\nNon-Implementation, If\napplicable\nOCAT\n2023\n2024 Fully\nImplemented\nOCAT\n2023\n2024 Fully\nImplemented\nCGSO\n2023\n2024 Fully\nImplemented\nAction Taken/Action to\nbe Taken\nThe OCAT is already in\nclose coordination with\nCGSO regarding the\nstatus of deliverles of\ngoods and services\nprocured by the City for\nrecording purposes\nThe OCAT already\nundertaken actions to\nproperly account the\npayables per Suppiler.\nThe OCAT Is already In\nclose coordination with\nCGSO regarding the\nstatus of dellverlas of\ngoods and services\nprocured by the City for\nrecording purposes\nOffice of the City\nAssessor\n2024\n2024 Ongoing\n3.16.1.2. Submit to the Auditor's Office the\nupdated coples of Tax Declaration as proof of\ncorrections/updates made to the 452 RPUs;\nOffice of the City\nAssessor\n2024\n2024 Ongoing\nThe City Assessor Office\nIs currently reviewing\nthe assessment levels\nof the purposes of\nproper RPT and SET\nImposition\nThe City Assesssor's\nOffice Is currently in the\nprocess of completing\nthe required Tax\nDeclarations for audit.\nAs of 31 July 2024, we\nare partially submitting\n85 adjusted Tax\nDeclaration. We commit\nto submit the lacking\ndocuments as soon as\npossible\n",
